{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he saw the calf and dancing.</b> Of all the musical instruments that were there, he mentioned only מחול (dancing), and the reason is that you will find in Scripture seven kinds of music, which correspond to the seven wandering stars, namely צ״ם חנכ״ל: כנור (lyre) corresponds to Saturn, תוף (timbrel) to Jupiter, מחול (dance) to Mars, מנים (stringed instruments) to the Sun, עוגב (flute/organ) to Venus, צלצלי שמע (clashing cymbals) to Mercury, תרועה (trumpet-blast) to the Moon. This is what is written (Psalms 150:3–4): ״הללוהו בתקע שופר הללוהו בנבל וכנור, הללוהו בתוף ומחול״; ״הללוהו במנים ועוגב״; ״הללוהו בצלצלי שמע הללוהו בצלצלי תרועה.״ Now among all of them there are nine kinds of music corresponding to the nine spheres, and the masters of the science of music know how to align each and every kind of these instruments with each and every sphere. And the שופר (shofar) and נבל (harp) that remain in the verse — the shofar corresponds to the ninth encompassing sphere, and the נבל corresponds to the eighth sphere, that of the stars. And because of this he mentioned מחול more than all the other instruments that were there in the matter of the calf, because the dance corresponds to the star Mars, for they were in the desert, a place of desolation and ruin over which this star holds sway. And this is why you find at the Sea (Exodus 15:20): ״ותצאן כל הנשים אחריה בתפים ובמחלת,״ for there were women there whose intent was not toward Heaven. And the תוף (timbrel) corresponds to the star Jupiter; this is what is written (ibid.): ״ותקח מרים הנביאה אחות אהרן את התוף בידה״ — he mentioned Aaron and attached the timbrel to him, because Aaron was entirely צדק (Jupiter/righteousness), in the manner of what is written (Job 29:14): ״צדק לבשתי וילבשני.״" "<b>However,</b> the Sages in their Midrash made of מחולות an expression from the root of מחילה (forgiveness). And the explanation of the matter is that of all the kinds of music that were in their hands, it happened for Moses that he saw from them only מחולות (dances), and this is a sign and token for the forgiveness that the Holy One, blessed be He, was destined to grant them for that sin, as they said, רז״ל: ״סימנא מילתא היא״ — it is a sign. And once Moses saw the sign, he hastened in the matter: ״ויקח את העגל אשר עשו וישרוף אותו באש ויזר על פני המים וישק וגו׳״ — the waters into which he ground it, he made them drink in a manner of humiliation, so that they would expel it through their bodily orifices, in the manner of what is written concerning idolatry (Isaiah 30:22): ״תזרם כמו דוה צא תאמר לו.״ And further, Moses intended to test them like suspected wives (סוטות), so that their faces would turn green and it would become known among them who rejoiced in his heart over that sin — for those who sinned and committed a deed, namely the worshippers, the sacrificers, and the offerers of incense among them, he judged them on the basis of witnesses and condemned them to death; but as for whoever rejoiced in his heart, they would not have known, and they needed to test them by means of the waters. This is what רז״ל interpreted: one who sacrificed and offered incense — by the sword; one who embraced and kissed — by death; one who rejoiced in his heart — by the הדרוקן (dropsy). And there are those who say: those for whom there were witnesses and warning — by the sword; witnesses without warning — that is death by plague; neither witnesses nor warning — by הדרוקן. Thus they interpreted in Yoma, chapter שני שעירי. And had the miracle of the הדרוקן occurred before them without drinking, it would have been an opening of the mouth for some of them to say that this punishment was on account of another sin; but once they drank, the matter was clear to them that the punishment was on account of this sin. And it says ״ויטחן״ (and he ground it), so that its ash would return to the likeness of the dust of the earth of the Tabernacle floor, which the priest would put into the water to make the suspected wife drink."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:37.079446884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}